WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.280
Token optimist turned mincemeat courtesy&nbsp;
of a particularly bloodthirsty "vampire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.720
bat," Glenn was a "Walking Dead" favorite.&nbsp;
So, come time for him to bite the dust,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.850
why was actor Steven Yeun so down to&nbsp;
say adios to his adored character?

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:19.437
"Hey you. Dumbass."

00:00:19.437 --> 00:00:23.520
Sweating, scared, and hopeless, Rick&nbsp;
Grimes is stuck in a tank surrounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.360
by walkers on all sides in the series&nbsp;
premiere of "The Walking Dead". He's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.720
not stupid. He knows he's finished,&nbsp;
until a voice comes in over the radio.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.020
"Yeah, you in the tank. Cozy in there?"

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.100
Before we learn who's behind the voice,&nbsp;
the camera zooms out over the city of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.960
Atlanta and the episode ends. Episode&nbsp;
2, however, wastes no time introducing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.320
this mysterious new character to us:&nbsp;
Glenn Rhee, played by Steven Yeun.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.760
Glenn became a fan favorite over the course&nbsp;
of the show, reminding viewers that there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.320
light even in the darkest of times. "The Walking&nbsp;
Dead" itself, however, doesn't play favorites,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.960
and Glenn meets his fate in the form of Negan's&nbsp;
bat Lucille at the beginning of Season 7. Yeun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.360
had no choice but to leave after that, seeing as&nbsp;
Glenn's demise was more than definitive. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.840
there's more to his departure than&nbsp;
just his character's untimely death.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.060
Steven Yeun spoke with fellow thespian&nbsp;
Riz Ahmed for Variety's Actors on Actors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.260
and naturally, "The Walking Dead" came up.&nbsp;
Being part of a series that big doesn't just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.980
vanish from the public consciousness when&nbsp;
an actor moves on to different projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:27.840
after all — especially when they play a character&nbsp;
as beloved as Glenn. It's an extremely special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.460
role to Yeun, but he also openly admitted that&nbsp;
he didn't mind leaving the character behind.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:38.400
Glenn is a "plucky, nice guy — nice to everybody,"&nbsp;
Yeun said, and, while he enjoys expressing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.260
part of himself as an actor, he was only able to&nbsp;
do it for so long before it got to him. Yeun said:

00:01:50.512 --> 00:01:53.700
From his perspective, that limited&nbsp;
where he was able to go as an actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.800
and being or feeling boxed in is the last&nbsp;
thing any actor wants; it was time to move on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.398
When the writers decided to&nbsp;
kill Glenn off, Yeun says:

00:02:02.398 --> 00:02:04.678
"There really wasn't much of a fight on my end."

00:02:04.678 --> 00:02:07.140
He added, however, that "it&nbsp;
was still sad" regardless.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.760
Since departing from post-apocalyptic&nbsp;
Georgia, Yeun has made the most of his time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.480
appearing in critically acclaimed projects&nbsp;
like "Sorry to Bother You," "Burning," and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.500
"Minari" — productions that allowed him&nbsp;
to explore roles other than the "genial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.860
natured guy." Fans will always&nbsp;
remember and miss Yeun as Glenn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.520
but it's a wonderful thing that he's been&nbsp;
able to expand his body of work elsewhere.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:31.440
In the years since his "Walking Dead" goodbye,&nbsp;
Steven Yeun has taken up some remarkable acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.880
opportunities. He's expanded his filmography&nbsp;
while trying out roles that, not too long ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.380
he likely wouldn't have had a chance at landing.&nbsp;
Nevertheless, in the eyes of many, he'll always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.060
be the man behind Glenn Rhee. With that in&nbsp;
mind, as "The Walking Dead" franchise expands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.260
in all directions, could we see Yeun return&nbsp;
to the role of Glenn in some form or fashion?

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:54.240
During a July 2022 appearance on the "Conan&nbsp;
O'Brien Needs a Friend" podcast, Yeun made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.460
it abundantly clear that the end of his "Walking&nbsp;
Dead" tenure was indeed the end. He told O'Brien:

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.760
This confirmed without a shadow of a&nbsp;
doubt that he's done with the Glenn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.220
role from here on out. Continuing, Yeun added:

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.860
Even though it would be cool to see Glenn Rhee&nbsp;
in the "Walking Dead" universe one more time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:25.020
don't get your hopes up that it'll happen. If his&nbsp;
comments and career trajectory prove anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:29.280
it's that Steven Yeun has left "TWD"&nbsp;
and his iconic character in the past.

